    "narrative": "The slate today is headlined by **Tyler Soderstrom**, our premier start with a 76.91 rating. Facing McGreevy, **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from an optimal lineup slot (#3 assumed) and a favorable pitching matchup (4.39 xERA). The combination of a strong park factor and a dynamic platoon advantage makes him our highest-ceiling play. **Brice Turang** (63.20) and **Josh Naylor** (61.99) also offer high-floor production; **Brice Turang** remains a critical component for our team-wide goals in stolen bases, and his position at the top of the lineup against Canning provides the run-scoring environment we covet.\n\nWhile the raw projections favor our core, we are exercising caution with several \"Lineup Pending\" designations. **Trevor Story** (45.72) and **Seiya Suzuki** (46.31) face elite arms in Luzardo and Sale, respectively, which suppresses their scoring potential. **Mickey Moniak** is the most precarious start today at 40.59; he barely clears the 40-point floor due to a severe platoon disadvantage against the lefty Montgomery and neutral park factors. **Cole Young** was the hardest omission from the starting nine, landing just short at 39.51; his projected #9 spot and lack of platoon upside ultimately relegated him to the bench in favor of higher-leverage opportunities.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the catchers, as **Dalton Rushing** (50.28) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (57.00) are heavily dependent on confirmed lineups. **Austin Riley** (50.81) carries some defensive upside regarding stolen base prevention against the opposing pitcher, though his matchup against the 3.43 xERA of Ben Brown makes him a marginal play. With **Giancarlo Stanton** sidelined and **Corbin Carroll** off today, the onus is on **James Wood** (55.32) to exploit the wind conditions and his lead-off spot to provide the speed-category boost Ghost Ride the WHIP requires to climb the standings.",
